## What the cheat sheet contains (read it all)

- North star + funnel order
- 10 non-negotiable rules (with **why** column)
- Full psychology → screen map (Welcome through tour, with lessons)
- Loading, trial ethics, offboarding
- Reference inspirations (Mine, Loom, SparkLoop, Grammarly, Hopper, Headspace, etc.)
- Printable per-screen audit grid (0–1–2 scoring)
- Metrics with target intuition
- Full principles glossary (27+ principles)
- Deep principles: Spark, loss aversion, priming, progressive disclosure, user-driven prompts, information overload, framing, personalization clarity, personalized paywall (+10%), Conway’s Law, reciprocity, Tim Cook / habits
- Grammarly 5 do’s, Hopper permissions, paywall rules
- Priority backlog + code owners
- Personal site vs in-app onboarding (not Framer)

## Hard rules (from cheat sheet — do not violate)

- Value before ask · endowment before trial
- One green CTA per screen (squint test)
- Real loss only post-activation — no fake urgency
- User-driven permissions — never pre-aha
- Personalized paywall: recap → map features → trial CTA
- Conway’s Law: one funnel owner, no duplicate collects
- Psychology only works if aha is **real** (live invoice, real booking link)
